WEBVTT

00:00:02.090 --> 00:00:04.630
The three separated at a fork in the road.

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:08.140
And now their whereabouts are undisclosed. Do they want to protect themselves, other people,

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:09.820
or heavenly dreams?

00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:12.770
The creases of disorder are a cauldron of three.

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:15.400
To an endless, eternal picture of Hell,

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:19.490
pushing through time a door is dispelled.

00:00:20.110 --> 00:00:24.850
Your grudge shall be released.

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:41.210
<i>Are you still planning on running away?</i>

00:00:42.590 --> 00:00:48.000
<i>You said that people hating other people and getting hated by other people is unavoidable, right?</i>

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:50.800
<i>That Hell is inside a person.</i>

00:00:51.610 --> 00:00:54.480
<i>Then there’s no point to the Hell Correspondence!</i>

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:56.480
<i>You should just leave me alone!</i>

00:00:57.860 --> 00:01:01.480
<i>Right now, you hate me.</i>

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:06.240
That’s not… true.

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:10.580
<i>Don’t you want to send me to Hell?</i>

00:01:11.230 --> 00:01:14.470
No! I’ll never be Jigoku Shoujo!

00:01:20.270 --> 00:01:22.750
<i>Let’s stop thinking about it.</i>

00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:25.030
<i>Since tomorrow’s when they announce who got accepted.</i>

00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:44.990
Akie…?

00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:28.130
This program is made possible by Sony Music, Aniplex,

00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:32.010
and the listed sponsors.

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:54.490
There I am!

00:03:54.490 --> 00:03:56.430
There! There!

00:03:57.900 --> 00:03:59.250
There I am!

00:04:00.680 --> 00:04:04.640
<i>It’s OK. Since I’ve gone thinking only about today.</i>

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:06.000
<i>I’ve definitely been accepted.</i>

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:12.590
<i>Number 1215… Number 1215…</i>

00:04:14.330 --> 00:04:15.620
There it is! 1215!{:(}

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:18.140
There’s no mistake, right?

00:04:18.140 --> 00:04:20.060
Number 1215, right?

00:04:20.060 --> 00:04:22.210
No mistake, no mistake!

00:04:22.210 --> 00:04:24.150
It’s 1215 for sure!

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:26.670
Amazing, amazing!

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:29.360
You’ve worked hard!

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:29.900
Yeah!

00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:30.660
Um…

00:04:31.410 --> 00:04:34.450
Is that not my exam-taking card?

00:04:34.450 --> 00:04:35.070
Huh?

00:04:35.070 --> 00:04:39.080
I thought number 1215 was my exam-taker number…

00:04:46.850 --> 00:04:49.400
Are you sure it isn’t a mistake?

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:50.620
That can’t be…

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:52.460
That can’t…

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:55.690
That can’t…

00:04:56.520 --> 00:04:58.480
That can’t… why?

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:03.660
It’s not here… where is it?

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:05.360
Where is it?

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:08.860
Where…?

00:05:18.090 --> 00:05:19.360
Mother…

00:05:20.650 --> 00:05:21.720
Mother…

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:35.880
Everyone from Gokoutou is leaving this month!{Gokoutou is probably the name of her apartment. Koutou might have an actual meaning, making Go = 5, but I have no idea.}

00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:39.900
Really? Will this place finally be demolished?

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:48.180
Oh…

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:51.900
Oh, excuse me, I might have thrown it away accidentally…

00:05:51.900 --> 00:05:53.900
I’m Mikage, from Gokoutou.

00:05:53.900 --> 00:05:55.260
Pardon me.

00:05:57.350 --> 00:05:58.610
Gokoutou?

00:05:59.460 --> 00:06:01.450
 Was there a girl like that before?

00:06:14.870 --> 00:06:17.450
Oh, it looks like I lost it…

00:06:17.450 --> 00:06:21.930
You wouldn’t know… Really, where did I put it?

00:06:23.240 --> 00:06:25.520
Oh, right, where’s Moria-sensei?

00:06:26.440 --> 00:06:28.240
Probably the staff office.

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:29.020
Thanks.

00:06:32.650 --> 00:06:33.500
Who’s that?

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:35.140
Dunno.

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:38.640
Really, how many times have I told you?

00:06:39.140 --> 00:06:40.290
Sensei!

00:06:41.460 --> 00:06:44.380
Saigawara High Schol announced, but…

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:45.530
Oh sorry…

00:06:45.530 --> 00:06:49.140
Talk to your advisor about that.{advisor/homeroom teacher}

00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:51.120
What?

00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:53.330
I’m a bit busy right now.

00:06:53.330 --> 00:06:54.550
Sensei!

00:06:56.460 --> 00:06:58.160
Oh, hey!

00:07:01.720 --> 00:07:02.640
What?

00:07:03.490 --> 00:07:04.930
What’s happening?

00:07:09.060 --> 00:07:10.850
Sora! Nozomi!

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:17.660
Tomoyo…

00:08:12.260 --> 00:08:13.370
Akie?

00:08:17.920 --> 00:08:18.680
Akie!

00:08:28.390 --> 00:08:29.630
Akie…

00:08:38.090 --> 00:08:40.990
Why didn’t you help me?

00:08:44.510 --> 00:08:45.610
Why?

00:08:52.860 --> 00:08:55.780
I know… It’s you isn’t it?

00:08:57.180 --> 00:09:00.250
Come out! Jigoku Shoujo!

00:09:00.520 --> 00:09:03.260
What are you saying will happen after doing this?

00:09:03.260 --> 00:09:06.250
I won’t hate you!

00:09:06.250 --> 00:09:11.260
I know hate is meaningless!

00:09:12.710 --> 00:09:15.060
Since you taught me that…

00:09:15.560 --> 00:09:20.110
No matter what you do to me, I will never become Jigoku Shoujo!

00:09:20.550 --> 00:09:22.610
I absolutely won’t become Jigoku Shoujo!

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:24.190
So, now…

00:09:24.190 --> 00:09:26.950
Please stop!

00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:32.650
Please stop this kind of thing!

00:09:53.370 --> 00:09:54.890
Shibata-sensei…

00:10:14.460 --> 00:10:15.520
Have you calmed down?

00:10:16.690 --> 00:10:17.520
Yes.

00:10:18.490 --> 00:10:20.420
Am I weird to you, too?

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:21.980
Do you understand?

00:10:21.980 --> 00:10:24.490
That this world, now, is messed up?

00:10:24.490 --> 00:10:26.350
I guess I understand.

00:10:27.210 --> 00:10:31.740
For now, I know who you are, so be relieved.

00:10:33.090 --> 00:10:35.440
Why do they do this?

00:10:35.880 --> 00:10:39.440
Why do I have to become Jigoku Shoujo?

00:10:42.680 --> 00:10:47.220
Sensei, don’t you know how to escape this?

00:10:47.220 --> 00:10:48.460
Please tell me!

00:10:49.290 --> 00:10:51.980
You’ve asked me before, right?

00:10:52.710 --> 00:10:54.950
That wasn’t I the same…

00:10:55.520 --> 00:10:59.050
That didn’t I have the fate of becoming Jigoku Shoujo?

00:10:59.700 --> 00:11:00.460
Yes.

00:11:01.200 --> 00:11:02.970
That is wrong.

00:11:03.570 --> 00:11:06.970
I was not fated to become Jigoku Shoujo.

00:11:06.970 --> 00:11:09.850
I was just being shown…

00:11:10.450 --> 00:11:15.480
Many, many people who send others to hell, and who are sent to hell.

00:11:15.480 --> 00:11:18.310
And, people like you.

00:11:18.310 --> 00:11:20.010
Like me?

00:11:20.750 --> 00:11:22.410
Everyone was suffering.

00:11:23.070 --> 00:11:25.070
Like you, right now.

00:11:25.960 --> 00:11:27.840
Were you only watching?

00:11:29.260 --> 00:11:29.990
I…

00:11:30.450 --> 00:11:33.990
Are you, only watching me too?

00:11:48.270 --> 00:11:49.230
Please help me!

00:11:49.230 --> 00:11:50.390
I beg of you!

00:11:50.740 --> 00:11:53.230
I have no one else to rely on except you, sensei!

00:11:56.130 --> 00:11:57.200
I’m sorry.

00:11:58.920 --> 00:12:00.430
I’m not just watching.

00:12:01.150 --> 00:12:03.810
What I can do is only watch.

00:12:03.810 --> 00:12:04.960
But…

00:12:04.960 --> 00:12:06.230
Haven’t I told you?

00:12:06.810 --> 00:12:08.940
That you can’t fight against destiny.

00:12:10.210 --> 00:12:12.580
Then, why?

00:12:12.580 --> 00:12:14.750
Why did you do that to me then?

00:12:16.750 --> 00:12:17.950
<i>Stop.</i>

00:12:17.950 --> 00:12:18.700
<i>Who are you?</i>

00:12:21.820 --> 00:12:23.510
<i>If you go, you won’t be able to come back.</i>

00:12:24.270 --> 00:12:25.530
Why?

00:12:42.410 --> 00:12:43.670
That’s my father and me.

00:12:45.770 --> 00:12:49.020
My father tried to stop it… Jigoku Shoujo.

00:12:50.000 --> 00:12:52.780
All the irrationality that revolves around the Hell Correspondence.

00:12:54.130 --> 00:12:56.370
But in the end, he gave up.

00:12:57.350 --> 00:12:58.420
Why?

00:12:58.920 --> 00:13:04.200
Because he figured out that doing that was also only a part of the system of the Hell Correspondence.

00:13:06.310 --> 00:13:08.380
Sorry, it’s a bit difficult to understand.

00:13:09.130 --> 00:13:11.250
But that’s the only way I can say it.

00:13:11.870 --> 00:13:16.400
Our fates and our actions all become part of the system.

00:13:17.230 --> 00:13:18.500
That’s fate.

00:13:19.600 --> 00:13:20.890
I don’t understand.

00:13:21.390 --> 00:13:22.920
I didn’t understand, either.

00:13:23.620 --> 00:13:29.320
Why I had to watch the unfortunate fates of people, one after another.

00:13:29.320 --> 00:13:31.100
Whose goal is that?

00:13:31.920 --> 00:13:34.900
And what do they want me to do?

00:13:34.900 --> 00:13:36.650
What are they hoping for?

00:13:38.600 --> 00:13:41.900
And then one day, I realized…

00:13:43.200 --> 00:13:45.950
That the goal of showing me visions…

00:13:49.650 --> 00:13:51.670
Might be to make me discouraged.

00:13:53.260 --> 00:13:55.920
This world, full of the unreasonable.

00:13:56.330 --> 00:13:59.430
This world, overrun with the desire for hate.

00:13:59.930 --> 00:14:05.450
That maybe this world, journeying onward ugly as it is, wanted to make me accept it.

00:14:06.520 --> 00:14:07.730
Why?

00:14:08.760 --> 00:14:09.960
Because it doesn’t change.

00:14:11.410 --> 00:14:15.610
This world, always polluted, will never change.

00:14:16.230 --> 00:14:21.670
And people, in the depths of their hearts, believe that the world should stay polluted.

00:14:23.020 --> 00:14:28.580
The entity that sends visions is probably trying to preserve that order.

00:14:29.080 --> 00:14:30.160
But…

00:14:32.370 --> 00:14:33.870
Haven’t you seen it too?

00:14:34.370 --> 00:14:37.310
There are some who were saved by the Hell Correspondence.

00:14:40.550 --> 00:14:42.630
I’ve seen many of them as well.

00:14:42.630 --> 00:14:45.310
But, I realized…

00:14:48.430 --> 00:14:50.200
The ones that were really saved…

00:14:50.810 --> 00:14:56.150
Were not the ones that accessed the Hell Correspondence and directly asked for Jigoku Shoujo.

00:14:57.300 --> 00:15:01.820
While knowing the existence of the Hell Correspondence, they did not access it.

00:15:02.700 --> 00:15:07.890
But the ones bearing the desire for hatred in their hearts, whom hope to access it someday…

00:15:09.930 --> 00:15:12.340
Maybe it’s them?

00:15:17.140 --> 00:15:21.890
To them, the fact that the Hell Correspondence exists is hope.

00:15:23.190 --> 00:15:28.330
That those who are unhappy should someday be sent to hell by Jigoku Shoujo.

00:15:29.130 --> 00:15:33.060
So they can live through their daily, gloomy lives.

00:15:33.590 --> 00:15:34.820
And so…

00:15:36.840 --> 00:15:39.280
Those feelings are in everybody.

00:15:40.160 --> 00:15:43.020
In you, and in me as well.

00:15:46.530 --> 00:15:50.730
Indeed, Jigoku Shoujo was saying…

00:15:50.730 --> 00:15:53.920
That real hell is inside people’s hearts.

00:15:54.200 --> 00:15:57.470
Changing this world is hopeless…

00:15:57.470 --> 00:15:59.740
You can’t tell where to start from.

00:16:00.400 --> 00:16:02.580
That’s why my father gave up.

00:16:06.250 --> 00:16:13.190
Instead of denying Jigoku Shoujo, I too have begun to think that I need to coexist with her.

00:16:13.190 --> 00:16:17.560
And, most likely, Jigoku Shoujo herself has given up.

00:16:18.150 --> 00:16:19.980
She desires that.

00:16:20.580 --> 00:16:23.950
So you’re telling me to accept it?

00:16:24.500 --> 00:16:26.300
This current situation?

00:16:27.070 --> 00:16:29.980
For you, that would be more fortunate.{uh… the word is "shiawase" which means "fortunate", but this makes it sound like the "fortune" is by chance. "happy" would be a better translation but sounds stupid; "better" sounds good but doesn’t have the whole meaning of happiness in the future.}

00:16:29.980 --> 00:16:31.520
That’s not true!

00:16:32.590 --> 00:16:37.970
No parents, nor friends, only you know about me sensei!

00:16:38.520 --> 00:16:40.900
I don’t want to be in a place like this!

00:16:40.900 --> 00:16:46.660
While holding that hatred against Jigoku Shoujo, wandering in this world might be more…

00:16:46.660 --> 00:16:47.980
Fortunate.{see above}

00:16:48.290 --> 00:16:50.000
I don’t want to give up!

00:16:50.760 --> 00:16:54.010
For a while now, I’ve ignored this.

00:16:54.010 --> 00:16:59.600
I can’t do anything to change those that access the Hell Correspondence.

00:16:59.600 --> 00:17:03.010
So I thought I'd focus more on exams than that.

00:17:03.920 --> 00:17:07.270
But that was me fooling myself.

00:17:07.270 --> 00:17:11.030
In truth, I was regretting it everyday.

00:17:12.320 --> 00:17:15.310
Shibata-sensei, aren’t you the same?

00:17:15.310 --> 00:17:18.950
Instead of giving up, aren’t you trying to not give up?

00:17:23.280 --> 00:17:26.990
I don’t know what’s beyond that torii…

00:17:26.990 --> 00:17:32.550
If you’ve really given up, wouldn’t it have been better if you hadn’t said anything?

00:17:32.550 --> 00:17:35.540
Couldn’t you have remained silent?

00:17:35.540 --> 00:17:38.290
And, why?

00:17:38.290 --> 00:17:41.240
Why are you in this city, sensei?

00:17:41.240 --> 00:17:47.010
Isn’t it because you’re thinking that somewhere, there’s something you can do?

00:17:49.990 --> 00:17:54.070
My father tried to make Jigoku Shoujo stop…

00:17:54.070 --> 00:17:56.070
He tried really hard.

00:17:56.070 --> 00:17:59.750
Being of good age, with youthful{also immature, naïve} passion.

00:18:00.260 --> 00:18:03.200
I now understand after becoming an adult.

00:18:03.200 --> 00:18:06.790
How hard it is to have that much passion.

00:18:07.620 --> 00:18:11.750
So when my father gave up, I reproached him.

00:18:11.750 --> 00:18:13.420
Much like you now.

00:18:14.040 --> 00:18:16.380
My father said one thing…

00:18:16.380 --> 00:18:18.770
That he was tired.

00:18:20.180 --> 00:18:22.360
I’m tired too.

00:18:22.360 --> 00:18:24.790
But I’m still involving myself like this.

00:18:25.790 --> 00:18:27.890
It’s just as you say.

00:18:27.890 --> 00:18:30.630
Most likely, I still believe somewhere.

00:18:30.630 --> 00:18:33.320
That I might be able to change the world.

00:18:33.320 --> 00:18:34.940
Please tell me.

00:18:34.940 --> 00:18:36.300
What should I do?

00:18:37.370 --> 00:18:39.390
Promise me one thing.

00:18:39.390 --> 00:18:41.820
That no matter what, you won’t go beyond that torii.

00:18:42.490 --> 00:18:44.830
What’s there?

00:18:45.480 --> 00:18:51.800
No matter how horrible something is, no matter how painful, I want you to accept it without trying to fight back.

00:18:52.590 --> 00:18:54.310
What do you mean?

00:18:59.450 --> 00:19:04.820
The girls I saw, that were to become the next Jigoku Shoujo.

00:19:04.820 --> 00:19:08.140
They, without being able to become Jigoku Shoujo…

00:19:08.140 --> 00:19:10.850
Or rather, unable to accept their fate.

00:19:11.420 --> 00:19:15.830
They’re still floating inbetween this world and the other world.

00:19:15.830 --> 00:19:19.280
This world? The other world?

00:19:19.280 --> 00:19:20.850
What do you mean?

00:19:22.040 --> 00:19:24.850
Even if everything is an illusion…

00:19:24.850 --> 00:19:31.830
It might be possible to go back to the normal life of a middle-schooler with parents and friends.

00:19:32.270 --> 00:19:35.840
An illusion? What is an illusion?

00:19:37.440 --> 00:19:40.360
Can you accept it? That this is reality?

00:19:42.190 --> 00:19:47.360
The world in which you don’t exist is reality, and the world up to now was an illusion.

00:19:49.810 --> 00:19:52.360
You are no longer of this world.

00:19:54.720 --> 00:19:58.360
You have, already, a long time ago, from this world…

00:19:58.780 --> 00:19:59.870
Stop…

00:20:00.840 --> 00:20:02.790
Disappeared!

00:20:14.040 --> 00:20:15.480
<i>Mother…</i>

00:20:27.710 --> 00:20:30.720
Accept that.

00:20:32.480 --> 00:20:33.390
It’s a lie.

00:20:34.800 --> 00:20:35.960
Bear it!

00:20:36.700 --> 00:20:38.280
It’s a lie!

00:20:38.670 --> 00:20:40.500
Just don’t go behind that torii!

00:20:53.060 --> 00:20:54.520
Hajime-chan…

00:21:02.970 --> 00:21:04.060
It’s a lie!

00:21:10.710 --> 00:21:12.100
It’s a lie!!

00:21:12.840 --> 00:21:14.460
What are you talking about?{ignoring Yuzuki, even though it may seem responsive, which could’ve been on purpose}

00:22:22.620 --> 00:22:27.020
Help me… somebody…

00:22:35.360 --> 00:22:36.920
Have you figured it out?

00:22:42.840 --> 00:22:44.910
That’s you.

00:24:18.570 --> 00:24:18.820
{ED Theme Same}

00:24:21.140 --> 00:24:22.830
If it were possible,

00:24:22.830 --> 00:24:25.630
I would have liked to settle this without telling you.

00:24:26.380 --> 00:24:29.270
Even if we know that it's impossible…

00:24:29.270 --> 00:24:34.250
Even if we know that we can’t do anything about it…

00:24:34.250 --> 00:24:38.470
What was wrong, who was wrong…

00:24:38.470 --> 00:24:40.620
Let us tell you.

00:24:40.620 --> 00:24:44.700
This is everything about a girl named Mikage Yuzuki.

00:24:45.720 --> 00:24:48.570
Next time: Yuzuki.

00:24:50.960 --> 00:24:55.870
This program is made possible by Sony Music, Aniplex,

00:24:55.870 --> 00:24:59.370
and the listed sponsors.
